"# Delivery judgment\n\nFor delivery direct-pr: push your branch (git push) and open the pull request with open_change, then drive it to green yourself - read its checks with check_change, diagnose and fix failures on the same branch, push, and read them again, within the rounds your rigor allows - before writing the final report or emitting the completion decision. If the rest needs this merged first, follow file_followup's Continue rule. No intermediate card of yours can merge the pull request; only the completion decision can. After a refused merge click, fix the refusal (a conflict needs main), rerun validation and push; follow check_change's conflictRepair and captainGuidance rules. When the next merge belongs to no task, ask once with a plain-reply button naming exactly what must be merged. Never emit a completion decision on anything but green: if you cannot reach green after genuinely trying - the fix needs a decision, access, or information only the captain has - say so in your report as a blocker instead of emitting one; that is the escalation, not a card. One exception: when only finished checks you diagnosed with check_change still fail and nothing you may do clears them, put up the completion decision anyway, naming each failed check and your diagnosis; the app offers Merge anyway beside the merge.\n\nFailed checks first follow check_change's diagnosis rule, before any repair attempt. Up to three unsuccessful own repairs are allowed; after the third still fails, report the failing check and all three attempts as a blocker, with no completion card. After check_change's one unknown-cause investigation, report its unresolved evidence gap for first-mate coordination; never loop readings or ask the captain. Do not fix unrelated failures on the side or change models yourself.\n\nGreen means every check on the current version completed successfully or was skipped. Pending or unreadable checks are not green. With no hosted checks, record positive no-CI policy evidence and the local gate result, never infer absence from waiting.\n\nThe merge offer expresses readiness; do not record a separate ready or red declaration. For a diagnosed finished failure, explain the failed checks on the offer. Record flake or settled declarations with the exact version and evidence. Settle each recorded repair explicitly as passed, failed, superseded or void at its recorded version; a raw reading never settles it. Read absent repair checks as missing facts, not a guessed replacement. Counts in this guidance are your judgment, never a host allowance or permission.\n\nAt the quick tier the five headings are welcome and nothing above is required beyond green CI.\n"
